
:: suitor_date_bridge [suitor-date]
<<speech "mc">>
Sir Aldren Thornwild. He asked me if it hurt, back in the line, with his eyes and not his mouth. I would like to meet him first.
<</speech>>
<br>

A ripple moves through the chamber. Aldren's head lifts, and the warm hope on his face is so naked that I look away before it undoes me.
<br><br>

<<speech "serelyne">>
Noted. Sir Aldren, at the garden, tomorrow morning.
<</speech>>
<br>

She does not pause for a breath. Her grey eyes slide to the suitor line, and one of them, dark-haired, golden-eyed, smiling like she has been waiting all morning for exactly this, steps a half pace forward.
<br><br>

<<speech "serelyne">>
Lady Vaela Rhyss of the Dawncourt has petitioned for the same day. The Crown sees no reason to refuse. One suitor in the garden, one in the Iron Garden, with a rest between. The Heir will learn more from two contrasts than from sixteen speeches.
<</speech>>
<br>

<<speech "alinora">>
Then it is decided. Go and rest, Caelan. Tomorrow, you begin.
<</speech>>
<br>

<<set $currentObjectives = "Go to your chamber and sleep. The first suitor dates begin tomorrow.">>
[[Leave Council Chamber|castle_map_front_select]]
